==> 239 prior non-numeric deps_hash refreshes (deps_hash moved, validated_at preserved).
    Counted from the manifest history, not from commit trailers — see the note above.

    This is EXPECTED, not a defect to fix by building option C. The classification in
    docs/completed/task-parity-staleness-diagnostic-seams.md found most refreshes are ordinary
    non-numeric edits to shared core files, NOT the inert diagnostic seams option C targets —
    and the recorded verdict was: DON'T build option C (it addresses a small minority while
    adding an invisible channel for a genuine numeric change to slip through), keep paying
    this small tax, and make the counter honest. The counter is now honest.

    Re-open option C only if the CLASSIFICATION shifts — i.e. refreshes start being dominated
    by inert diagnostic seams. The raw count alone is not that signal and never was.
